<Project>

  <!-- Assert that restore actually AUDITED every project, rather than merely
       succeeding.

       Why this file exists, and why it is not in Directory.Build.props: NuGet's
       restore target runs at the SOLUTION level, so the output properties below
       are not visible to a file that projects import. Directory.Solution.targets
       is MSBuild's solution-level extensibility point and must sit beside the
       .sln.

       What it defends against: a green restore is not proof that an audit
       happened. NU1900 ("error communicating with package source while getting
       vulnerability information") is a warning, so an unreachable advisory
       source degrades the audit to silence and the build stays green. A
       vulnerability gate that has quietly stopped running looks exactly like a
       clean repository. RestoreProjectsAuditedCount is the only mechanical
       distinction between the two.

       Requires MSBuild 17.13 / .NET SDK 9.0.200 or later, and is NOT populated
       under static graph restore. Both cases leave the properties empty, which
       would make this check silently vacuous - the exact failure it exists to
       catch - so an empty value is an explicit error rather than a pass.

       Audited + skipped must equal the total: an incremental restore legitimately
       skips up-to-date projects, and those are not re-audited. CI restores from a
       clean tree, so the skipped count is normally zero there.

       Proven to fail before being trusted green: with -p:NuGetAudit=false the
       audited count drops to 0 against 3 projects and this target errors. -->

  <Target Name="AssertRestoreAuditedEveryProject"
          AfterTargets="Restore"
          Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">

    <Error Condition="'$(RestoreProjectCount)' == '' Or '$(RestoreProjectsAuditedCount)' == '' Or '$(RestoreSkippedCount)' == ''"
           Text="Cannot verify that the NuGet audit ran: restore did not report its audit counts (RestoreProjectCount='$(RestoreProjectCount)', RestoreProjectsAuditedCount='$(RestoreProjectsAuditedCount)', RestoreSkippedCount='$(RestoreSkippedCount)'). These need MSBuild 17.13 / .NET SDK 9.0.200 or later and are not populated under static graph restore. Failing rather than passing vacuously." />

    <Error Condition="'$(RestoreProjectCount)' != '$([MSBuild]::Add($(RestoreProjectsAuditedCount), $(RestoreSkippedCount)))'"
           Text="Restore did not audit every project in the solution. Audited $(RestoreProjectsAuditedCount) and skipped $(RestoreSkippedCount) of $(RestoreProjectCount) projects. An unaudited project is an ungated dependency graph - check the restore log for NU1900 (advisory source unreachable) before assuming this is a tooling problem." />

  </Target>

</Project>
